---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Link from '../../components/Link.astro';
import { routes } from '../../lib/links';
import { EDITORIAL_TEAM, type BreadcrumbItem } from '../../lib/schema';

const breadcrumbs: BreadcrumbItem[] = [
  { label: 'Home', route: routes.home() },
  { label: 'Privacy, Cookies & Terms', route: routes.privacyCookiePolicy() },
];
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Privacy, Cookies & Terms | Statohub"
  description="Statohub's privacy policy, cookie policy and terms of use: what we collect, the cookies we use, how Google AdSense advertising works here, and your ad choices."
  canonicalPath={routes.privacyCookiePolicy()}
  breadcrumbs={breadcrumbs}
>
  <article class="max-w-3xl">
    <p class="page-kicker">Policy</p>
    <h1 class="page-title">Privacy, Cookies & Terms</h1>
    <div class="article-prose">
      <p>
        This page explains how Statohub handles privacy, cookies, and browser
        storage, and sets out the <a href="#terms">terms</a> on which the site
        may be used. Statohub is a static statistics education and calculator
        site. We do not provide user accounts, sign-in areas, comments, or user
        profiles.
      </p>
      <p><strong>Last updated:</strong> September 20, 2026</p>

      <h2>Privacy Policy</h2>

      <h3>What we collect and do not collect</h3>
      <p>
        Statohub does not ask you to create an account, sign in, or submit
        personal profile information. Calculator inputs are processed in your
        browser by client-side code and are not intentionally sent to Statohub as
        calculator submissions. We do not sell personal data. The site does use
        analytics, described under <a href="#analytics">Analytics</a> below, and
        does carry third-party advertising, described under
        <a href="#advertising">Advertising</a> below.
      </p>

      <h3>Hosting and server logs</h3>
      <p>
        Statohub is served through Cloudflare Pages. Like most web hosts and
        content delivery networks, Cloudflare may process standard request data
        such as IP address, requested URL, user agent, timestamp, and basic
        security or performance signals in edge logs. These logs are used for
        operating, securing, and delivering the site.
      </p>

      <h3 id="analytics">Analytics</h3>
      <p>
        Statohub uses two analytics services to understand aggregate site usage,
        such as which pages are read and where visitors arrive from. We do not
        use analytics data to build advertising profiles, and we do not sell
        personal data.
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li>
          <strong>Google Analytics 4</strong> (measurement ID
          <code>G-PVHDLYC7T4</code>) sets first-party cookies in your browser --
          typically named <code>_ga</code> and <code>_ga_*</code> -- to tell
          repeat visits apart and to measure traffic sources. It may also
          process your IP address, device and browser type, and the pages you
          view. Google's description of how it handles this data is at
          <a href="https://policies.google.com/technologies/partner-sites"
            >policies.google.com/technologies/partner-sites</a
          >.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Ahrefs Web Analytics</strong> is a page-view measurement
          script which, according to Ahrefs, does not use cookies and does not
          track individuals across sites.
        </li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        You can opt out of Google Analytics on every site you visit by
        installing Google's
        <a href="https://tools.google.com/dlpage/gaoptout"
          >Google Analytics Opt-out Browser Add-on</a
        >, or by blocking cookies for this site as described under
        <a href="#control-cookies">How to view and control cookies</a>.
      </p>

      <h3 id="advertising">Advertising</h3>
      <p>
        Statohub carries advertising served by Google AdSense. Ad revenue is what
        pays for the site and keeps every article and calculator free to use.
      </p>
      <p>
        Third-party vendors, including Google, use cookies and similar
        technologies to serve ads on this site. Google's use of advertising
        cookies enables it and its partners to serve ads to you based on your
        visits to Statohub and to other sites on the internet. Google and its
        ad-technology partners may also process technical data such as your IP
        address, device and browser type, and the page you are viewing, in order
        to select an ad, measure whether it was seen, cap how often you see the
        same one, and detect invalid traffic.
      </p>
      <p>
        Statohub does not send your calculator inputs, or anything else you type
        into a page, to advertisers. Ad selection happens entirely inside Google's
        systems: we do not receive, see, or store the personal data those partners
        process, and we cannot read the cookies they set.
      </p>
      <p>
        Google's own description of how it uses data from sites that use its
        services is at
        <a href="https://policies.google.com/technologies/partner-sites"
          >policies.google.com/technologies/partner-sites</a
        >.
      </p>

      <h3>Your advertising choices</h3>
      <p>
        You can turn off personalised advertising from Google at
        <a href="https://adssettings.google.com/">Google Ads Settings</a>. To opt
        out of personalised advertising from many other vendors at once, use
        <a href="https://optout.aboutads.info/">optout.aboutads.info</a> or, in
        Europe,
        <a href="https://www.youronlinechoices.eu/"
          >youronlinechoices.eu</a
        >. You can also block or delete advertising cookies directly in your
        browser -- see <a href="#control-cookies">How to view and control
        cookies</a> below.
      </p>
      <p>
        Opting out does not remove ads from the site. It means the ads you see are
        chosen without using an advertising profile built from your browsing.
      </p>

      <h3 id="consent">Consent in the EEA, the UK, and Switzerland</h3>
      <p>
        If you are in the European Economic Area, the United Kingdom, or
        Switzerland, advertising cookies are set only after you agree to them.
        Consent is collected through a Google-certified consent management
        platform, which shows a message the first time you visit and records
        your choice in your browser so you are not asked again on every page.
      </p>
      <p>
        The analytics cookies described under
        <a href="#analytics">Analytics</a> above are not yet wired into that
        consent message. Until they are, you can prevent them by using the
        Google Analytics opt-out add-on linked in that section, or by blocking
        cookies for this site in your browser.
      </p>
      <p>
        You can change or withdraw that choice at any time using the privacy or
        consent settings link the message provides, or by clearing this site's
        data in your browser, which makes the message appear again on your next
        visit. Withdrawing consent does not affect processing that already
        happened while consent was in place.
      </p>

      <h3>Third-party links</h3>
      <p>
        Some pages link to external educational or reference sites. Those sites
        are controlled by their own operators and are covered by their own
        privacy notices. Statohub is not responsible for the content or privacy
        practices of third-party sites.
      </p>

      <h3>Children's privacy</h3>
      <p>
        Statohub is an educational website for general audiences. It is not
        designed to collect personal information from children, and we do not
        knowingly collect personal information from children.
      </p>

      <h3>Changes to this policy</h3>
      <p>
        We may update this page when the site changes, when we add or remove
        services, or when legal requirements change. The updated date above will
        reflect the latest revision.
      </p>

      <h3>How to contact us</h3>
      <p>
        For privacy questions, including anything about advertising cookies or
        your consent choice, email
        <!--email_off--><a href={`mailto:${EDITORIAL_TEAM.email}`}>{EDITORIAL_TEAM.email}</a><!--/email_off-->.
        The <Link to={routes.contact()}>contact page</Link> explains what else
        that address is for.
      </p>

      <h2>Cookie Policy</h2>

      <h3>What cookies are</h3>
      <p>
        Cookies are small text files that websites can store in your browser.
        They are commonly used for sign-in sessions, preferences, security,
        analytics, and advertising.
      </p>

      <h3>Cookies set by Statohub</h3>
      <p>
        Statohub sets no cookies of its own for advertising or profiling. The
        first-party cookies you may find on this domain are set by Google
        Analytics -- typically <code>_ga</code> and <code>_ga_*</code> --
        described under <a href="#analytics">Analytics</a> above. They hold an
        anonymous identifier used to count visits, not a profile built from
        personal details you have given us.
      </p>
      <p>
        The site's dark-mode preference is stored with browser localStorage
        under the key <code>theme</code>. localStorage is not a cookie, and this
        preference stays on your device unless you clear it in your browser. The
        remaining cookies you will encounter on Statohub come from Google's
        advertising stack and from our host, described next.
      </p>

      <h3>Advertising and consent cookies</h3>
      <p>
        Google and its ad-technology partners may set cookies, or use similar
        browser storage, in order to serve ads, measure whether an ad was seen and
        acted on, limit how often you see the same ad, and detect fraud and
        invalid traffic. These are third-party cookies set by domains such as
        <code>googlesyndication.com</code>, <code>doubleclick.net</code>, and
        <code>google.com</code> -- not by Statohub -- so we can neither read them
        nor delete them for you.
      </p>
      <p>
        The consent management platform also stores your consent choice in your
        browser. That record is what keeps the consent message from reappearing on
        every page, so clearing it will bring the message back.
      </p>
      <p>
        Where consent is required -- in the EEA, the UK, and Switzerland --
        advertising cookies are set only after you agree to them. See
        <a href="#consent">Consent in the EEA, the UK, and Switzerland</a> above
        for how to change your choice, and
        <a href="#advertising">Advertising</a> for the opt-out links.
      </p>

      <h3>Cookies from hosting and security services</h3>
      <p>
        Our CDN or host may set cookies or use similar browser storage when
        needed for security, performance, abuse prevention, or network delivery.
        These controls help keep a static site available and protected.
      </p>

      <h3 id="control-cookies">How to view and control cookies</h3>
      <p>
        You can view, block, delete, or limit cookies in your browser settings.
        Most browsers also let you clear localStorage and other site data for a
        specific domain. Blocking some host or security cookies may affect how a
        site loads or whether protective checks work correctly. Blocking
        third-party cookies specifically will stop the advertising cookies
        described above without affecting the calculators, which run entirely in
        your browser.
      </p>

      <h2 id="terms">Terms of Use</h2>
      <p>
        By using Statohub you agree to these terms. They are short because the
        site is simple: there is nothing to sign up for, nothing to buy, and
        nothing you submit is stored.
      </p>

      <h3>Educational use only</h3>
      <p>
        Statohub teaches statistical methods and provides calculators that run
        them. The content is general educational material. It is not medical,
        legal, financial, or other professional advice, and it is not a
        substitute for a qualified statistician or adviser who can see your
        actual data and circumstances. Decisions you make based on what you read
        or compute here are your own.
      </p>

      <h3>Accuracy</h3>
      <p>
        We work hard to get the maths right: every guide is reviewed before
        publication, every calculator is covered by automated tests, and we
        correct errors when they are reported. Our
        <Link to={routes.editorialPolicy()}>editorial policy</Link> sets out
        how. Even so, the site is provided "as is" and we cannot promise that
        every page is free of error or that a calculator is suitable for your
        particular purpose. Check that a method fits your data before you rely
        on its result, and please <Link to={routes.contact()}>tell us</Link>
        if something is wrong.
      </p>

      <h3>Calculators</h3>
      <p>
        The calculators run in your browser and are provided for learning and
        for checking your own working. You are responsible for the numbers you
        enter and for how you use the output. We may change, add, or remove a
        calculator at any time.
      </p>

      <h3>Content and copyright</h3>
      <p>
        The guides, worked examples, calculator code, and design of Statohub are
        the property of Statohub unless otherwise stated. You are welcome to
        read, print, and use the material for personal study and teaching, to
        link to any page, and to quote short passages with attribution and a
        link back to the source page. Republishing whole guides, scraping the
        site to build a competing dataset or product, or presenting our content
        as your own is not permitted without our written permission.
      </p>
      <p>
        External references cited in the guides, such as the NIST/SEMATECH
        e-Handbook or OpenStax textbooks, belong to their respective publishers
        and are used under their own licences.
      </p>

      <h3>Third-party sites and advertising</h3>
      <p>
        Pages link to external educational and reference sites, and the site
        carries advertising served by Google AdSense. We do not control those
        sites or the advertisers, and a link or an advertisement is not an
        endorsement. Your dealings with any third party are between you and
        them.
      </p>

      <h3>Acceptable use</h3>
      <p>
        Do not use the site in a way that interferes with its operation or with
        other people's use of it, including automated requests at a rate that
        degrades the service, attempts to bypass security or advertising
        controls, or use of the content to train or build products in breach of
        the copyright terms above.
      </p>

      <h3>Limitation of liability</h3>
      <p>
        To the fullest extent permitted by law, Statohub and its editorial team
        are not liable for any loss or damage arising from your use of, or
        inability to use, the site or its calculators, or from reliance on any
        content on it. Nothing in these terms limits liability that cannot be
        limited by law.
      </p>

      <h3>Changes</h3>
      <p>
        We may update these terms when the site changes. The updated date at the
        top of this page reflects the latest revision, and continued use of the
        site after a change means you accept the revised terms.
      </p>
    </div>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>